---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';

const title = 'Terms of use';
const description =
  'The terms you accept by using trendingprompt: how prompts and images may be reused, what is not warranted, and how disputes are handled.';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: title,
  description,
  url: `${SITE.url}/terms`,
  dateModified: '2026-08-11',
};
---
<BaseLayout title={`${title} — trendingprompt`} description={description} schema={schema}>
  <section class="shell page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="page__title">Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      By using {SITE.legalName} you accept these terms. Last reviewed {SITE.policyUpdated}.
    </p>

    <div class="page__body prose">
      <h2>Using the site</h2>
      <p>
        The site is provided free of charge for personal and commercial reference. You may read it,
        copy prompts from it, and link to it. You may not scrape it at a volume that degrades it for
        others, republish it wholesale, or present its guides as your own work.
      </p>

      <h2>Prompt text</h2>
      <p>
        Prompt text published here is free to use, modify and publish, commercially or otherwise,
        with no attribution required. That is the purpose of the site. Short functional strings of
        this kind attract little or no copyright protection in most jurisdictions, and no claim is
        made over them.
      </p>

      <h2>Images</h2>
      <p>
        Images are generated output, published as evidence that a prompt produces what it claims.
        Their legal status is not simple and is not settled the same way everywhere:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Rights in AI-generated images depend on the terms of the tool that produced them. Those
          terms differ between tools and between paid and free tiers, and they change.
        </li>
        <li>
          Several jurisdictions, including the United States, decline copyright protection for
          material lacking human authorship. An image here may therefore be protected only in part,
          or not at all.
        </li>
        <li>
          Before reusing an image commercially, check the current terms of the tool named on the
          entry. Do not rely on this site's publication of an image as a licence to use it.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Written material — the guides, the notes, the descriptions — is the site's own work and is
        protected by copyright. Quote it with a link; do not republish it in full.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party names</h2>
      <p>
        Midjourney, DALL·E, Stable Diffusion, Adobe Firefly and other tools named on this site are
        the trademarks of their respective owners. This site is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
        sponsored by any of them. Names are used descriptively, to say which tool produced a result.
      </p>

      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The site is provided "as is". Generative models are non-deterministic and change without
        notice: a prompt that reproduced faithfully when it was tested may produce something
        different after a model update. No guarantee is made that any prompt, parameter or technique
        described here will work, keep working, or be suitable for your purpose.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing here is legal advice. Statements about copyright and licensing are general
        background, not a substitute for advice from a qualified lawyer in your jurisdiction.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, {SITE.legalName} is not liable for any loss or damage
        arising from use of this site or of anything published on it, including any commercial
        decision taken on the basis of a prompt, guide or licensing statement found here.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising and links</h2>
      <p>
        The site carries third-party advertising and links to external sites. Neither an ad nor a
        link is an endorsement, and this site is not responsible for the content, products or
        practices of any third party. See the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> for how
        advertising affects your data.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        These terms may be updated as the site changes. Continuing to use the site after a change
        means accepting the revised terms; the review date above indicates when they last changed.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions, or notice of anything that should not be here:
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. Takedown procedure is on the
        <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
